  "worked_solution": "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}(2-\\frac{3}{{y}^{2}})\\text{d}y={\\int }_{-2}^{-1}(2-3{y}^{-2})\\text{d}y\n$$\n\nThen, we split the integral into the difference of two integrals and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}(2-3{y}^{-2})\\text{d}y & =2{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}\\text{d}y-3{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}{y}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2y\\,{|}_{-2}^{-1}-3(-{y}^{-1}){|}_{-2}^{-1} \\\\  & =2y\\,{|}_{-2}^{-1}+3\\cdot \\frac{1}{y}{|}_{-2}^{-1} \\\\  & =2(-1-(-2))+3(\\frac{1}{(-1)}-\\frac{1}{(-2)}) \\\\  & =2(-1+2)+3(-1+\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =2(1)+3(-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =2-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
